  "observations": [
    "Real native JWKS client refused a CA-trusted certificate for the wrong hostname before HTTP and succeeded after the issuer certificate was repaired.",
    "Actual v2/v3 routes required valid bearer credentials; bad signature, issuer, audience, expiry, not-before and malformed values failed.",
    "Fresh HTTPS handshakes were required for hot CA removal: empty socket_opts was insufficient on OTP27; the accepted artifact uses a nonempty harmless socket option and disables SSL session reuse.",
    "Hot bearer replacement preserved the actual native hub PID and project checkpoint; issuer signing-key retirement then rejected the old token after refreshed JWKS while the new token passed.",
    "Both local durable materialization and actual broker group next offsets advanced from1to2 without resetting; the acknowledged old delivery did not reappear.",
    "Expired-bearer and missing-CA preflight failed without activation; postrotation wrong/missing/malformed/private-key trust inputs failed without changing current config.",
    "Full shutdown logs were checked for all synthetic bearer values, keystore password and private-key PEM markers; owned containers, networks and volumes were removed."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Proxy-to-broker lane is separately private plaintext; SASL_SSL/SCRAM example is not enabled or runtime-qualified here.",
    "No principal propagation, RBAC, MDS fallback, per-token broker ACLs or automatic issuer token acquisition is selected.",
    "Kubernetes evidence is read-only rendering, not a live secured pod rollout.",
    "JWT replacement is not issuer revocation; retired-key checks depend on issuer/validator JWKS cache policy.",
    "Failed exploratory runs are ignored and excluded from success evidence; early handshakes that reused prior TLS sockets were explicitly rejected as qualification evidence.",
    "Application remains Apache-2.0; external Confluent Enterprise/trial dependencies and production entitlement requirements are separate."
  ]
}
